    "result_text": "A hold no longer takes a claim out of claimed, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\nHow it works now, for a hold on a person or on a single claim:\n- **Still counted:** the person's claimed figure, the claimed-total, and the `claimed=` and `claimed-total=` fields in the ROLLUP and TOTALS audit lines all include a held claim's amount.\n- **Still left out while held:** the due figures \u2014 due-total, overdue, the settled/open split, aged, period, tag and month totals.\n- **Unchanged:** a deferred claim still leaves claimed, and so does an open claim of someone whose retirement date the sheet's today has reached. A claim bound by a statement still counts in full.\n\nChanges:\n- **Server:** a new `Person.countsClaimed(...)` applies the old counting rule without the hold check. `RollupService` now adds a claim's amount to claimed whenever that check passes, and only then skips held claims for the due figures (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/rollup/RollupService.java`).\n- **Front end:** `countsClaimed` in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts` now ignores holds and only checks deferral and retirement. That one check feeds both the person's claimed figure and the claimed-total.\n- I updated the doc comments on `Claim.held` and `ClaimService.toggleHold` to say a held claim stays claimed.\n\nNo stored data or schema needed changing. The only other places that add up claimed are those two front-end figures.",
